 ## Table of Contents
 
+The portable NTFS composition prechecks standing grants through its native helper. Broad Everyone/logon write allowances and links outside the workspace reject the grant before modification. Protected private children retain their DACLs without disabling unrelated commands. A current-user-owned root may gain only that user’s non-inheriting WRITE_OWNER right to set the required label; ownership and other accounts stay unchanged. Interrupted inheriting grants are completed on reuse. The portable runner supplies workspace/temp locations for the Python restricted-token mkdir compatibility hook. Token construction and retained standing grants follow upstream; these checks do not eliminate concurrent replacement races or provide read or network confinement.
+
